  "about": "Istanbul bank / CBRT EFT closures. Law 2429 fixed holidays; May 1 from 2009 (Law 5892); Jul 15 from 2017 (Law 6752); Ramazan Bayramı (3 days) and Kurban Bayramı (4 days) on the Diyanet calendar, with the eve (arife) and Oct 28 holidays from 13:00 (banks and EFT run in the morning: early_close, counted open, but Borsa Istanbul/Takasbank do not settle on these half days). No weekend substitution. Government 9-day 'extensions' are administrative leave (idari izin) for public servants only: banks, EFT and Borsa Istanbul operate, so they are not closures. Islamic dates from the Diyanet-derived table in python-holidays, checked against Borsa Istanbul's 2026 holiday announcement and published 2024-2026 dates. Kurban 2006-12-31..2007-01-03 spans years, so its weekdays (2007-01-01 to 03) are exceptions. Coverage 2005-2027.",
